  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Linking Agribusiness and Nutrition in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve the diet intake and nutritional practices in target beneficiaries (Infant and Young Child Feeding practices, hygiene, breastfeeding, water and sanitation) in the Beira corridor in Mozambique and promote the local production of Ready to Use Therapeutic Foods. This will target 623,000 beneficiaries and contribute to delivering MDG 1.C on reducing hunger. Key stakeholders (GoM, private sector and donors) influenced through credible, evidenced based models for effective nutrition interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
